<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Levedi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">9th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Levedi was an early leader of the Hungarians, described by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantine-vii">Constantine VII</a> as the first of their voivodes when they lived under the authority of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khazar-khaganate">Khazar Khaganate</a>. The Khazar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khagan">khagan</a> gave him a noble Khazar wife and offered to make him prince of the Hungarians. He declined in favour of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almos">Álmos</a> or his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arpad">Árpád</a>, the founder of the ruling dynasty.</p></div>
